This libdraw is 9front's (the Plan2001 CPU server's, 1.10.2026; 9front is
MIT-licensed), one library for drawterm's kernel and for the Plan 9
programs built as WebAssembly on it (../../../wasmapp): drawterm's own
libdraw was an older subset of it with its own draw.h, and two Display
structs - drawterm's had no usrlock - broke a program linked with both.
The headers are 9front's too (../include: draw.h, event.h, mouse.h,
keyboard.h), without Plan 9 C's #pragma lines; RWLock is in lib.h, the
kernel's.

Not 9front's: mkwarp.c (drawterm's: 9front's needs geometry.h); chan.c
has isspace renamed xisspace (it would be ctype's).
Changed here: stringbg.c - its op parameters Drawop, not int (Plan 9's C
takes an enum for an int, clang does not); event.c - its slaves (mouse,
keyboard, timer, estart) are kprocs, not forked processes: there is no
fork; no notes either.
Not built (Makefile NOTHREAD): enter getrect keyboard menuhit mouse
newwindow readcolmap - libthread, rio's newwindow, libbio; there are
none of them here.  Not here: warptest.c and test.c, tests.
